WEBVTT

00:48:29.204 --> 00:48:32.371
I had to make a decision that caused
me and another person pain,

00:48:32.829 --> 00:48:35.496
but I'm better for it. And
it's not sad anymore.

00:48:35.496 --> 00:48:40.954
It was it was actually the the golden key
that opened the door to to my liberation.

00:48:41.288 --> 00:48:44.204
And there was loss in that. But
but there was more gain.

00:48:44.204 --> 00:48:45.663
You know, it became a gift in the end.

00:48:45.663 --> 00:48:49.371
Like, very often I think how memoir
writing is almost like

00:48:49.746 --> 00:48:51.246
the process of therapy, right.

00:48:51.246 --> 00:48:52.996
Where you go back there and you say, well,

00:48:52.996 --> 00:48:57.204
who was that person and why did she do
this and think this and love these people

00:48:57.204 --> 00:49:02.913
and leave these people. And there's always
an answer if you're willing to dig